  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.8.3 -- an additive, non-breaking release: two new form-level helpers, focus on every control, two new field parameters, a two-way-bindable EditRadioEnum \"Other\" field, and two attribute-handling contracts widened to cover every control that can use them.\n\nNEW\n- FormAutoSave: one component replacing per-field @bind-Value:after wiring for a whole form. Subscribes once to the EditContext, debounces changes (DebounceMilliseconds, default 500ms trailing) into one OnSave call carrying the changed fields. SaveWhenInvalid/Concurrency/ShouldSave/TimeProvider round out the configuration. OnSaveFailed hands back the fields a failed save was carrying -- they return to the front of the pending set and retry on the next flush instead of being lost; unwired, the exception re-dispatches for an ErrorBoundary.\n- FormDefaults.FocusFirstField (bool?, default off): focuses a form's first rendered field once, after the scope's first render -- the form-level counterpart to the new FocusOnFirstRender below. Skips disabled/readonly/hidden fields, yields to an explicit FocusOnFirstRender on a specific control, retries up to 10 render batches for async-loaded forms, and needs no IJSRuntime registration to safely no-op.\n- Public FocusAsync() and FocusOnFirstRender (bool, default false) on every Edit* control -- programmatic and declarative focus of whichever element a Tab into the control would land on. Never focuses a disabled/read-only/hidden control. Named FocusOnFirstRender, not AutoFocus, so a native autofocus attribute still splats through untouched.\n- Suggestions (IEnumerable<string>?) on EditString/EditNumber: renders an open-vocabulary <datalist> hint, distinct from a Select control's closed vocabulary.\n- LabelContent (RenderFragment?) on every control: rich-markup label content (icon plus text, etc.) in place of a plain Label string.\n- EditRadioEnum<TEnum>: bind the \"Other\" free-text box two-way with @bind-OtherValue -- gives it a real FieldIdentifier, EditContext registration, and validation-summary participation.\n\nCHANGED\n- Event-handler chaining: a splatted onclick/onkeydown/onmousedown on EditRange, both date pickers, Modal/Drawer, and Select now chains with the control's own same-named handler instead of one discarding the other.\n- The null-attribute-erasure fix (a splatted attribute surviving when the control has no opinion on it) now covers EditTextArea, EditDateNative, the EditSelect family, EditBool, and EditRange -- previously only EditString/EditNumber had it.\n\nFIXED\n- Every control's read-only rendered value now carries aria-describedby (description/tooltip/error text), previously reachable only in edit mode.\n- EditCheckedEnumList/EditCheckedStringList's read-only fieldset and EditColor's read-only row are now correctly nameable to assistive tech.\n- ToastQueue: an intermittent ObjectDisposedException race in Pause/Resume/Remove/Clear.\n- FormDefaults no longer requires an IJSRuntime registration, fixing a crash under HtmlRenderer/out-of-band rendering (email templates, PDF export).\n- AttributeSplat.RestExcept: a case-variant withheld attribute (e.g. aria-Label) is now actually removed instead of leaking a duplicate.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog",
